From 68765424627d1ecf8ec9bde761c04110a8639e5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wayne Maurer <wmaurer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:55:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] feat(foldkit): type produced Blocks from one producer
 verdict

Definitions gain produceBlock and produceViewlessBlock. The method name
selects view presence, and the Definition's OutMessage Schema selects
OutMessage presence, so the produced shape never reads the producer.
owner, Model, and OutMessage come from the Definition. Every other member
is mapped over the completed Block contract's keys and reads one cached
verdict: the producer's completed Block, or an InvalidBlockProducer that
names the reason. The verdict rejects a producer that is not a nullary
function, returns any or never, belongs to another Definition, disagrees
on view or OutMessage presence, or adds or drops members.
